ions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T20:09:23-08:00","id":1363239,"title":"","content":"I convinced him that \u201cintimacy\u201d means actual sex and that just messing around shouldn\u2019t trigger the Frailty. Thanks \ud83d\ude0a. Ttyl.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-25T00:17:44-08:00","id":1363262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1363229-how-can-i-convince-my-st-that-this-doesn\u2019t-trigger-the-mantle-of-the-maiden-frailty#post1363229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My Swan Maiden character met someone she really likes last session. She has the chance to make out with him tonight and she\u2019d like to go further than kissing, but she doesn\u2019t want to be unable to regain Willpower for three days (especially since she\u2019s low as it is). Any advice?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well... there is one possibility...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=j8ZF_R_j0OY\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=j8ZF_R_j0OY\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=j8ZF_R_j0OY </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=j8ZF_R_j0OY\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=j8ZF_R_j0OY </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-25T06:56:24-08:00","id":1363292,"title":"","content":"Ewwwwwww!!!!<br /> <br /> No! I didn\u2019t mean that. I meant like touching each other. Or maybe oral. Anyway, I got the ST to agree that it didn\u2019t count as \u201cintimacy.\u201d And yeah, I know it probably sounds stupid written down in black and white, but it was important to my character.<br /> <br /> And that\u2019s bullshit. Anal is so forbidden by the Bible. It\u2019s called \u201csodomy.\u201d I\u2019m not Christian, but I remember that from Sunday school.<br /> <br /> But thanks. You defo made me laugh \ud83d\ude02.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-25T18:29:38-08:00","id":1363380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1363229-how-can-i-convince-my-st-that-this-doesn\u2019t-trigger-the-mantle-of-the-maiden-frailty?p=1363292#post1363292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that\u2019s bullshit. Anal is so forbidden by the Bible. It\u2019s called \u201csodomy.\u201d I\u2019m not Christian, but I remember that from Sunday school.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Well it depends. Some definitions of Sodomy require two males to be involved. Others consider it any sexual act that cannot lead to procreation(anal, oral etc). This is made especially fun with Sodomy laws being on the books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-25T19:25:19-08:00","id":1363385,"title":"","content":"Didn\u2019t the Supreme Court abolish those?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-03T20:04:13-08:00","id":1365166,"title":"","content":"'Intimacy' could be about intent. Full sex can be very non-intimate with the right people. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />{","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-03T21:13:06-08:00","id":1365174,"title":"","content":"True! My friend who\u2019s playing a satyr said the same thing, that if my character was just horny, she could probably even go all the way without triggering the Frailty because it wouldn\u2019t be \u201cintimate,\u201d but our ST wouldn\u2019t go for it, so we ended up using the argument that just messing around doesn\u2019t count. My character (Corenice) does kind of like the guy, but he\u2019s not Kithain or even Kinain, plus she\u2019s terrified of falling in love cause of the whole Dark Fate thing.<br /> <br /> Thanks \ud83d\ude0a","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-07T18:19:19-08:00","id":1366194,"title":"","content":"With Swan Maidens, &quot;going further than kissing&quot; probably triggers the frailty... You can talk to your ST, but I think you're fundamentally misunderstanding the Kith. Even kissing can be extraordinarily intimate, and the point of the Swan Maiden is to maintain her &quot;purity&quot;. You keep asking how to bypass this frailty, but being sexual in basically any form is as antithetical to Swan Maidens as being dishonorable is to Trolls. Their inability to have sexual pleasure is the point of the Kith. Asking how to be sexual without triggering the Swan Maiden Frailty is like asking how to never help people in need as a Boggan, or how to be a Clurichaun without a horde. Swan Maidens keep it in their pants, or they lose willpower. Anything beyond that is a house rule.<br /> <br /> As for legality, there are plenty of extremely normal sexual acts (Including even oral in some states) that are &quot;illegal&quot;, but only because our country's base laws were made by Puritans. In some states, even pre-marital sex is illegal. Nobody is ever going to go to jail for having consensual anal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25663,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25663-rigelj","user":"RigelJ","date":". 02-07-2020, 09:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25663-rigelj","name":"RigelJ","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-07T19:15:34-08:00","id":1366210,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25663-rigelj\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25663\" data-vbnamecard=\"25663\">RigelJ</a> I know. I just wanted to have my cake and eat it too. Or at least my character did. Luckily I really am pretty good at arguing and convincing people.<br /> <br /> However, on a less self-centered level, I wanted to redefine the Swan Maiden kith as being about monogamy instead of purity. And sometimes while you\u2019re searching for the ultimate happy monogamous relationship with your True Love, you end up messing around with a few other people along the way.<br /> <br /> To be honest, I liked the part about the kith being good at giving romantic advice. I like sidhe and satyrs too, but my friend is playing a satyr and I\u2019ve played a sidhe before. I wanted to try something new.<br /> <br /> What do you think of my interpretation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-07T20:01:43-08:00","id":1366219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1363229-how-can-i-convince-my-st-that-this-doesn\u2019t-trigger-the-mantle-of-the-maiden-frailty?p=1366210#post1366210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25663-rigelj\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25663\" data-vbnamecard=\"25663\">RigelJ</a> I know. I just wanted to have my cake and eat it too. Or at least my character did. Luckily I really am pretty good at arguing and convincing people.<br /> <br /> However, on a less self-centered level, I wanted to redefine the Swan Maiden kith as being about monogamy instead of purity. And sometimes while you\u2019re searching for the ultimate happy monogamous relationship with your True Love, you end up messing around with a few other people along the way.<br /> <br /> To be honest, I liked the part about the kith being good at giving romantic advice. I like sidhe and satyrs too, but my friend is playing a satyr and I\u2019ve played a sidhe before. I wanted to try something new.<br /> <br /> What do you think of my interpretation?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Its a mixed bag, though an interesting one for sure. To start, I can see not wanting to step on your friends turf, in terms of not all playing the same Kith. As for trying to reinterpret Swan Maidens, I actually would agree. I think they are a little bit too far from the beaten path, with more birthrights and frailties than they should have. The Dark Fate frailty is an absolutely BRUTAL frailty (and good on you for being scared of it). Swan Maidens don't need the other frailty on top of it. I would have tweaked them a bit personally, let them have sex and lose one of their Birthrights. As for a Monogamy focus, I can certainly see the merit of having a Changeling whose core ethos stems from a desire to embody fealty or love for a single person, though I would personally have just played a Fiona Troll, or a Troll with the Troubadour legacy at that point. Alternatively, to take a page from the players guide, I think a Lycian who embodies Monogamy could be interesting.<br /> <br /> I will say that it's a bit of a loaded discussion for me, because I see the concept of sexual &quot;purity&quot; as a way of controlling people, and, from my subjective viewpoint, think it's actually evil. Swan Maidens embody an idea I actually think hurts real people. It enforces the Slut/Prude double standard, and tells people that virginity is something they should be very concerned about, both telling men they are unfit if they are virgins, and women that there is something wrong with them if they choose to explore that part of themselves. I know way too many people my age who put knives to their bodies because they had been sexually assaulted and felt that they were no longer pure for it. I had a friend who I would console as she cried at night because her mother kept calling her a whore, despite the fact that she had never been with anyone sexually, as if that should somehow make a difference. Swan Maidens are an idea that the patriarchy puts onto people, and its wrong. <br /> <br /> Now, to be clear, Changeling is a horror game, and f*ck if that isn't horror. Remember that Changeling is all about conflicting natures, and is ultimately a game about tragedy; if the Changeling you are demands this idea of sexual purity, but the human you are KNOWS that sex isn't intrinsically dirty or impure, that's an internal conflict that can be a great character arc. In a world where Swan Maidens exist, yeah, I actually think your interpretation is the only way a Swan Maiden could survive. The question is whether we want those ideas informing our culture, or whether those are stories that should maybe be left to the mists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25663-rigelj","name":"RigelJ","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-07T20:18:50-08:00","id":1366224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RigelJ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1363229-how-can-i-convince-my-st-that-this-doesn\u2019t-trigger-the-mantle-of-the-maiden-frailty?p=1366219#post1366219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know way too many people my age who put knives to their bodies because they had been sexually assaulted and felt that they were no longer pure for it. <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. I know.<br /> <br /> Thanks for listening. You\u2019re one of the very few guys I\u2019ve talked to who uses the word patriarchy without being ironic or sarcastic. Night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-08T05:37:10-08:00","id":1366300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RigelJ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1363229-how-can-i-convince-my-st-that-this-doesn\u2019t-trigger-the-mantle-of-the-maiden-frailty?p=1366194#post1366194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With Swan Maidens, &quot;going further than kissing&quot; probably triggers the frailty... You can talk to your ST, but I think you're fundamentally misunderstanding the Kith. Even kissing can be extraordinarily intimate, and the point of the Swan Maiden is to maintain her &quot;purity&quot;. You keep asking how to bypass this frailty, but being sexual in basically any form is as antithetical to Swan Maidens as being dishonorable is to Trolls. Their inability to have sexual pleasure is the point of the Kith. Asking how to be sexual without triggering the Swan Maiden Frailty is like asking how to never help people in need as a Boggan, or how to be a Clurichaun without a horde. Swan Maidens keep it in their pants, or they lose willpower. Anything beyond that is a house rule.<br /> <br /> As for legality, there are plenty of extremely normal sexual acts (Including even oral in some states) that are &quot;illegal&quot;, but only because our country's base laws were made by Puritans. In some states, even pre-marital sex is illegal. Nobody is ever going to go to jail for having consensual anal.</div> </div> </div> </div>shit I know but if they must not be able to have casual hookups at least make it sure you or your lover don't suffer a fate worst then death.<br /> <br /> and seriously the Puritians where jerks that left Dutch because they where too tolerant<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T06:14:27-08:00","id":1366753,"title":"","content":"So my character (Corenice) has been spending more time with the guy she likes, and last session while they were making out (just kissing this time) she admitted to him that she was catching feels for him and he admitted the same thing back. Our ST decided that was enough to trigger True Love's Curse (I do have the True Love Merit so the Frailty does apply), and I have till the next session to decide if I want the Dark Fate Flaw to apply to my character or her beloved. Corenice is a very unselfish person, especially when she's in love, so I'm probably gonna decide that I should get the Dark Fate. I'm not looking to dodge it or anything, I understand that the Swan Maiden is a kith that represents the inevitable tragedy of True Love, but I've never played a character with the Dark Fate Flaw before. Do you guys have any advice or suggestions for dealing with it short of my character giving up the guy she loves?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T06:19:14-08:00","id":1366755,"title":"","content":"Is their anyway to stop the Dark Fate flaw? I think a Moirae could have some advice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T07:18:20-08:00","id":1366766,"title":"","content":"That's a great idea! Thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T08:07:38-08:00","id":1366978,"title":"","content":"Dive head first into it! There's no point taking flaws if they don't show up in play, so make the most of it and see where it goes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25078-brickman","name":"Brickman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T09:56:26-08:00","id":1367015,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25078-brickman\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25078\" data-vbnamecard=\"25078\">Brickman</a> thanks! I think I'm gonna do that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T09:23:38-08:00","id":1367550,"title":"","content":"I personally tend to be a very solution oriented person, especially as a player, while as a Storyteller, I tend to enjoy leveraging irony, and setting it up so that players make the bed they sleep in, real Monkey's Paw type narratives. If I was a PC who knew I had dark fate (and I assume she does) I would talk to my ST about how my character might (try to) get around it, with the knowledge that I am astronomically more likely to fail than to succeed. Were I in this position as an ST, I would do one of two things. I would either set up a quest within the Deep Dreaming wherein the Motley need partake in several physical, mental and emotional trials, and gain some Spring related magic to dampen the effects of Dark Fate; the Spring art has removal of curses and doom within it's wheelhouse, so that would be my first thought. In all likelihood, trying to stop the Dark Fate would be part of what causes it, unless my players got REALLY creative, AND lucky. Further, failure would likely cause ripple effects, hurting not only the Swan Maiden and her lover, but the Motley at large, perhaps tearing apart the group itself and inflicting the fate upon all of them rather than just the one. Bad things can happen when you swim against fate, though if anyone can light the dark and bring back Spring, its Changelings. My second solution as a player (though it feels like cheating) would be an epic quest to learn Naming <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 </span></span> and forgo my identity as a Swan Maiden. Were I a storyteller and a player had such a plan, I would try to set a trap wherein success in this regard would in fact bring about my player's Dark Fate before she could accomplish her goals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25663-rigelj","name":"RigelJ","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T10:03:52-08:00","id":1367556,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25663-rigelj\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25663\" data-vbnamecard=\"25663\">RigelJ</a> thank you!!! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> These are both great ideas. I'm gonna suggest the first one to my ST (and the other players) if he doesn't think of it first. And yeah, I know trying to stop it might end up being the very thing that makes it happen, but it's better than my character just (metaphorically) falling on her sword and accepting her fate.<br /> <br /> I'm not gonna try the Naming thing, because who she is is really important to my character's identity, plus there's the very real risk that the person she loves won't feel the same way if she's not a Swan Maiden anymore, but it's still a really good idea. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T16:13:38-08:00","id":1367638,"title":"","content":"Shit certain people deal a lot of Fate like the Moirae? Maybe you can Quest to find a wise Fae scholar?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T20:14:11-08:00","id":1367674,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m gonna look for a Moirae. Where can I read up on them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T10:25:09-08:00","id":1367807,"title":"","content":"denizens of the dreaming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T12:06:40-08:00","id":1367828,"title":"","content":"Thank you. I think I actually own that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T21:05:00-08:00","id":1370224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1363229-how-can-i-convince-my-st-that-this-doesn\u2019t-trigger-the-mantle-of-the-maiden-frailty?p=1367556#post1367556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> thank you!!! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> These are both great ideas. I'm gonna suggest the first one to my ST (and the other players) if he doesn't think of it first. And yeah, I know trying to stop it might end up being the very thing that makes it happen, but it's better than my character just (metaphorically) falling on her sword and accepting her fate.<br /> <br /> I'm not gonna try the Naming thing, because who she is is really important to my character's identity, plus there's the very real risk that the person she loves won't feel the same way if she's not a Swan Maiden anymore, but it's still a really good idea. Thanks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Making your partner stop loving you because you\u2019re no longer a Swan Maiden is a super good point, that would hit that ironic tragedy feel SUPER well. Good catch","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25663-rigelj","name":"RigelJ","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T07:34:40-08:00","id":1370350,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25663-rigelj\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25663\" data-vbnamecard=\"25663\">RigelJ</a> thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T12:20:10-08:00","id":1370424,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25663-rigelj\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25663\" data-vbnamecard=\"25663\">RigelJ</a> we found one of the Moirae and talked to her. In return for her helping us, I had to swear an oath that I would not harm or help my Motley harm any of the Adhene (the Denizens) for the next seven years unless they attack me first. First, we (my character's Motley) have to travel to the Deep Dreaming and bring back an item that represents the Platonic ideal of sacrifice. Then we have to perform a ritual using one of the Twelve Treasures of Britain as a focus which will cleanse Corenice and her boyfriend of the Dark Fate. Finally, I have to sacrifice something truly precious to me to prevent him from dying when the Dark Fate discharges its power in one last spasm before it's finally neutralized. Plus we have other plots and subplots that don't involve me to resolve before we get to this. Tbh, I'm really worried that she'll have to give up her Swan Maidenhood to save her boyfriend as the final step (the Moirae lady kind of hinted at that).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T13:13:07-08:00","id":1370430,"title":"","content":"thats so cool!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T18:38:21-08:00","id":1370480,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23952_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23952\" data-vbnamecard=\"23952\">Konradleijon</a> ikr!!! \ud83e\udd70 I really like this character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T19:09:23-08:00","id":1372080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1363229-how-can-i-convince-my-st-that-this-doesn\u2019t-trigger-the-mantle-of-the-maiden-frailty?p=1365174#post1365174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True! My friend who\u2019s playing a satyr said the same thing, that if my character was just horny, she could probably even go all the way without triggering the Frailty because it wouldn\u2019t be \u201cintimate,\u201d but our ST wouldn\u2019t go for it, so we ended up using the argument that just messing around doesn\u2019t count. My character (Corenice) does kind of like the guy, but he\u2019s not Kithain or even Kinain, plus she\u2019s terrified of falling in love cause of the whole Dark Fate thing.<br /> <br /> Thanks \ud83d\ude0a</div> </div> </div> </div>Corenice needs to get her Sarah Conner on. &quot;There is no fate but what we make.&quot;<br /> <br /> Meanwhile this whole Dark Fate could have been avoided she'd just gone with God's Loophole. Figure if God can't see that kind of sex neither can your ST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","user":"johntfs","date":". 02-29-2020, 10:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-01T04:42:21-08:00","id":1372129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1363229-how-can-i-convince-my-st-that-this-doesn\u2019t-trigger-the-mantle-of-the-maiden-frailty?p=1372080#post1372080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Meanwhile this whole Dark Fate could have been avoided she'd just gone with God's Loophole. Figure if God can't see that kind of sex neither can your ST.</div> </div> </div> </div>True lol. My one friend used to sprinkle a line of salt in front of her bedroom door because she thought God couldn\u2019t see in if she did that. But Corenice is a Swan Maiden and it really makes her happy being in love. She\u2019d just rather not have to die or lose her kith\u2014her identity\u2014because of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-01T14:01:04-08:00","id":1372187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1363229-how-can-i-convince-my-st-that-this-doesn\u2019t-trigger-the-mantle-of-the-maiden-frailty?p=1372129#post1372129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True lol. My one friend used to sprinkle a line of salt in front of her bedroom door because she thought God couldn\u2019t see in if she did that. But Corenice is a Swan Maiden and it really makes her happy being in love. She\u2019d just rather not have to die or lose her kith\u2014her identity\u2014because of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who says she'll die? Figure in the WoD there's plenty of &quot;Dark Fates&quot; that make death seem like a mercy. Your &quot;Dark Fate&quot; could easily to be &quot;you kill the one you Truly Love.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's been a <i>long</i> time since I looked at <i>Changeling: The Dreaming (</i>I much prefer Changeling: The Lost for my WoD faerie tales), but is there some kith/path/aspect that's associated with motherhood? Maybe instead of having Corenice try to cling to her Swan &quot;Maidenhood&quot; she should lean into the idea of the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Triple_Goddess_(Neopaganism)\" target=\"_blank\">Triple Goddess </a>by embracing the idea of the Mother. Instead of avoiding your Dark Fate, have her pursue a destiny that does all that and more. Don't run away, run toward.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-01T16:57:15-08:00","id":1372204,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2318\" data-vbnamecard=\"2318\">johntfs</a> She\u2019s not pregnant! lol<br /> <br /> But aside from that, you make some really good points. I need to think about this. And talk to my friend; she\u2019s been playing WoD longer than I have. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T07:07:41-08:00","id":1372265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1363229-how-can-i-convince-my-st-that-this-doesn\u2019t-trigger-the-mantle-of-the-maiden-frailty?p=1372204#post1372204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2318\" data-vbnamecard=\"2318\">johntfs</a> She\u2019s not pregnant! lol<br /> <br /> But aside from that, you make some really good points. I need to think about this. And talk to my friend; she\u2019s been playing WoD longer than I have. Thanks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ones of the reasons that I posted &quot;The Loophole&quot; video is that your thread really put me in the mind of the girls in the video. They want the social acceptance of being &quot;good Christians, but they don't want the risks/sacrifices of leading the actual Christian life (as they see it). So they're up for doing anal because it &quot;technically&quot; preserves their &quot;virginity.&quot; Likewise, you want to play a &quot;Swan Maiden&quot; but you also don't/didn't want to deal with actually having the taboos/frailties that come with that Kith. You want your character to be able to fuck without other stuff coming down.<br /> <br /> It'd be like somebody coming to me as an ST and saying &quot;I want to play a Gangrel vampire because I like the claws and turning into a Wolf, but can I make an some kind of alchemist so I can make a potion to let him walk around in sunlight?&quot; And my answer would be &quot;No. He's a vampire. Sunlight burns vampires. If you want to do the wolf/claw thing, play a werewolf instead.&quot;<br /> <br /> So, my overall take for you is, instead of trying to push your ST into ignoring the rules of the Kith, play a Kith that lets you do what you clearly want to do. Maybe a Selkie.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T09:25:47-08:00","id":1372291,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=johntfs;n1372265]<br /> <br /> Ones of the reasons that I posted &quot;The Loophole&quot; video is that your thread really put me in the mind of the girls in the video. They want the social acceptance of being &quot;good Christians, but they don't want the risks/sacrifices of leading the actual Christian life (as they see it). So they're up for doing anal because it &quot;technically&quot; preserves their &quot;virginity.&quot; Likewise, you want to play a &quot;Swan Maiden&quot; but you also don't/didn't want to deal with actually having the taboos/frailties that come with that Kith. You want your character to be able to fuck without other stuff coming down.<br /> <br /> Yeah, basically.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'm happy with the way her character development is going. Thank you for your advice.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]}]}